{"hits": {"hits": [{"links": {"bibtex": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/277567?format=bibtex", "latex-eu": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/277567?format=latex-eu", "latex-us": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/277567?format=latex-us", "json": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/277567?format=json", "json-expanded": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/277567?format=json-expanded", "cv": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/277567?format=cv", "citations": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A277567"}, "created": "1989-04-21T00:00:00+00:00", "updated": "2023-03-07T02:53:33.011420+00:00", "metadata": {"authors": [{"full_name": "Sivers, Dennis W."}], "publication_info": [{"journal_volume": "41", "artid": "83", "year": 1990, "page_start": "83", "journal_title": "Phys.Rev.D"}], "texkeys": ["Sivers:1989cc"], "abstracts": [{"value": "When one takes into account the transverse momenta of the constituents in a polarized proton, there exists a kinematic, \"trigger-bias,\" effect in the formulation of the QCD-based hard-scattering model which can lead to single-spin production asymmetries. It seems convenient to represent the coherent spin-orbit forces in a polarized proton by defining an asymmetry in the transverse-momentum distribution of the fundamental constituents. It may then be possible to organize the hard-scattering model so that the kinematic constraints of hard 2 \u2192 2 scattering provide the leading contribution at large transverse momentum to asymmetries of the type ANd\u03c3(hp\u2191\u2192jet+x), ANd\u03c3(hp\u2191\u2192``\u03c0''x), where p\u2191 denotes a transversely polarized proton and \"\u03c0\" represents any spinless meson composed of light quarks. This approach provides testable relationships between different asymmetries."}], "control_number": 277567, "dois": [{"value": "10.1103/PhysRevD.41.83"}], "titles": [{"title": "Single Spin Production Asymmetries from the Hard Scattering of Point-Like Constituents"}, {"title": "POINT - LIKE"}], "author_count": 1, "document_type": ["article"]}, "id": "277567"}], "total": 1}, "links": {"self": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?sort=mostcited&q=j%20Phys.Rev.D%2C41%2C83&size=3&page=1&fields=control_number,titles.title,authors.full_name,author_count,publication_info,arxiv_eprints.value,dois.value,texkeys,abstracts.value,document_type,imprints,isbns,collaborations.value", "bibtex": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?sort=mostcited&q=j%20Phys.Rev.D%2C41%2C83&size=3&page=1&format=bibtex", "latex-eu": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?sort=mostcited&q=j%20Phys.Rev.D%2C41%2C83&size=3&page=1&format=latex-eu", "latex-us": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?sort=mostcited&q=j%20Phys.Rev.D%2C41%2C83&size=3&page=1&format=latex-us", "json": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?sort=mostcited&q=j%20Phys.Rev.D%2C41%2C83&size=3&page=1&fields=control_number,titles.title,authors.full_name,author_count,publication_info,arxiv_eprints.value,dois.value,texkeys,abstracts.value,document_type,imprints,isbns,collaborations.value&format=json", "json-expanded": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?sort=mostcited&q=j%20Phys.Rev.D%2C41%2C83&size=3&page=1&format=json-expanded", "cv": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?sort=mostcited&q=j%20Phys.Rev.D%2C41%2C83&size=3&page=1&format=cv"}}